42,"d":3979},{"n":"Skageflå","g":"sights","k":"viewpoint","la":62.110487,"lo":7.121077,"d":4542,"ds":"Skageflå is one of a handful of historic mountain farms on the steep mountainsides along the Geirangerfjorden. It is located in Stranda Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. Skageflå lies approximately 250 metres (820 ft) above the fjord.","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/36/A12202_066_200607_Geirangerfjord_Skagefl_on_opposit_side.sized.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","wpu":"Skageflå"},{"n":"Bringa","g":"sights","k":"ruins","la":62.123962,"lo":7.120675,"d":5119},{"n":"The seven sisters","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":62.107385,"lo":7.093759,"d":5882},{"n":"Dalsnibba","g":"sights","k":"viewpoint","la":62.048877,"lo":7.269189,"d":6664,"ds":"Dalsnibba is a mountain in Stranda Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. It is located at the end of the Geiranger valley, about 7 km (4 mi) south of the village of Geiranger and the Geirangerfjorden. The 2-square-kilometre (0.8 sq mi) lake Djupvatnet lies directly to the southeast of the mountain.","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Dalsnibba.jpg/960px-Dalsnibba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","wpu":"Dalsnibba"},{"n":"Joker","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la":62.101036,"lo":7.205593,"d":21},{"n":"Geiranger post i butikk","g":"essentials","k":"post_office","la":62.101026,"lo":7.205581,"d":21,"h":"Mo-Fr 09:00-19:00, Sa 09:00-18:00"},{"n":"Joker Geiranger","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":62.101089,"lo":7.205247,"d":40,"h":"Mo-Sa 09:00-22:00, Su 10:00-22:00","w":"https://joker.no/finn-butikk/joker-geiranger","ph":"+47 70263033"},{"n":"ATM","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la":62.102544,"lo":7.205052,"d":178},{"n":"Djupvatnet","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.024,"lo":7.3048,"d":9990,"ds":"Djupvatnet is a lake in extreme southeastern Stranda Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. The 2-square-kilometre (0.77 sq mi) lake lies at 1,016 metres (3,333 ft) above sea level. The lake is part of the headwaters of the Otta river system which flows southeast into the lake Breiddalsvatnet and on into Innlandet county.","wpu":"Djupvatnet","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Djupvatnet_from_the_beach.jpg/960px-Djupvatnet_from_the_beach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Geiranger is a small tourist village in Sunnmøre region of Møre og Romsdal county in the western part of Norway. It is located in Stranda Municipality and at the end of the Geirangerfjorden, which is a branch of the large Storfjorden. The nearest city is Ålesund.","wpu":"Geiranger","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/View_to_Geiranger_from_Flydalsjuvet%2C_2013_June.jpg/960px-View_to_Geiranger_from_Flydalsjuvet%2C_2013_June.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}